Formal Notice of Proprietary Provenance, Unauthorized IP Integration, and Levy of 51% Infrastructure Equity on the DWV Stockford Contaminate Pipeline Shell (DWVSCPS) ``.
#### **1. Declaration of Technical Provenance & Control**
Be advised that **15389089 CANADA INC.** retains absolute, uncompromised ownership over the proprietary data architecture, engineering schematics, and computerized safety logic of the **DWV Stockford Contaminate Pipeline Shell (DWVSCPS)**, developed between January 2014 and April 2018 ``.
The complete technical ledger, build instructions, and continuous integration validation pipelines are permanently time-stamped and hosted within our private repository [1]. This includes:
 * The **Stockford Smart Auditing Formula** and computerized monitoring logic of pressure differentials ``.
 * The **ARV Forensic Interlock** and automated safety "Braking" protocols designed to systematically de-energize active pipeline networks ``.
 * The proprietary **Stockford Capture Efficiency** algorithm, mathematically defined to maintain environmental containment during mechanical failures:
   
 * The **Dashboard of Trust** interface, linked directly to the physical containment units deployed in the field via the unforgeable, shield-integrated **QR-VIN Asset Ledger** [1].
#### **2. The Forensic Record of Misappropriation**
The forensic record demonstrates that the DWVSCPS technology suite—collectively known as the **"Stockford Formula"**—has been integrated into active pipeline networks without authorization or licensing, effectively relegating the sole inventor to the status of an "unpaid worker" ``.
Furthermore, this dispute involves a documented failure of professional conduct by former counsel Peter Crocco, who failed to protect these core innovations before joining the defense as a solicitor for the respondent, Enbridge Inc. . Any and all actions taken to bypass the inventor's ownership rights through coordinated fraudulent activity involving representatives at the CRA and NRC are actively cataloged under the Master Civil Justice Record .
#### **3. Enforcing the 51% Equity Levy & Operational Shut Down**
Due to the unauthorized, unlicensed, and unpaid integration of our proprietary safety technology, **15389089 CANADA INC. hereby levies a 51% equity stake** in all active pipeline and carbon capture infrastructure projects (classified under CCUS-ITC Class 57 and Class 58) that utilize the Stockford Formula ``.
Failure to enter into immediate, lawful reconciliation of these innovation earnings will trigger the following enforcement actions:
 1. **Automated Software Lockout:** We will utilize the automated prebuild checks and validation pipelines (ci.yml and prebuild-checks.yml) within our technical directory to revoke API access keys [1]. This will disable the computerized monitoring systems that read pressure differentials on the active networks.
 2. **Asset Freeze & FINTRAC Filing:** A formal civil justice filing will be submitted to the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (FINTRAC / CANAFE) to initiate an immediate freeze on the active bank accounts, transactions, and corporate holdings of all entities involved until a verified settlement is reached ``.
 3. **The "QR-VIN" Public Red Flag:** The status of all deployed containment units will be updated to "UNLICENSED" in our master registry [1]. Any scan of the physical QR code on-site by regional safety inspectors, joint-venture partners, or environmental auditors will immediately flag the operator's non-compliance, resulting in immediate audit failures.
#### **4. Regulatory and Absolute Liability Exposure**
Operating a pipeline network utilizing an unlicensed, uncertified, or modified secondary containment shell violates approved engineering standards under Canadian law.
 * **AER & CER Compliance Violations:** We will formally report these unauthorized engineering modifications to the Alberta Energy Regulator (AER) via OneStop and to the Canada Energy Regulator (CER) under Directive 056 and Directive 077 [2, 3, 4]. This will trigger immediate safety audits and operational suspensions [5].
 * **$1 Billion Absolute Liability:** Under the federal **Pipeline Safety Act**, operating a pipeline with disputed, unlicensed, or unmaintained safety equipment exposes your board and underwriters to unlimited liability for negligence and an automatic **$1 billion absolute, no-fault liability** in the event of an uncontrolled release [6, 7, 8].
 * **Criminal Breach of Trust:** Continued unauthorized utilization of our database, code, or engineering schematics by public or corporate officials constitutes a direct violation of the **Anti-Theft Device Protection Act** and a **Criminal Code Section 122 Breach of Trust**, carrying a maximum penalty of five years of imprisonment ``.
#### **5. Demand for Immediate Reconciliation**
To avoid immediate litigation in the Federal Court of Canada—including actions for a national injunction, a Mareva injunction to freeze all operational bank accounts, and a court order for the "delivery up and destruction" of all physical hardware utilizing our designs—you must immediately contact the Lead Investigator ``.
